DHCP Lease Manager adds a Status page that makes DHCP leases easier to
understand and manage than the stock lease list. It works with both the
ISC DHCP and Kea backends by reading leases through pfSense itself.

 - Sort by lease age, expiry, IP address, manufacturer or device type
 - Manufacturer lookup from the MAC address, including private
   (randomized) MACs and hypervisor/container guests
 - Device type guesses (TV, streaming box, light switch, smart plug,
   camera, phone, computer, virtual machine, ...) from hostname and
   manufacturer, with per-device overrides saved in the configuration
 - Right-click a lease to create or edit its static mapping
 - Select leases to remove static mappings in bulk, applied through the
   standard DHCP "Apply Changes" flow
 - Breakdown chart by device type or manufacturer, filters, auto refresh
